## a session-tag refusal
   ✋ ahbode.prep — the role TRUSTS this box, and refuses what its session carries (sts:TagSession)
      ⇒ an IAM Roles Anywhere session carries a source identity and session tags,
        and a chained AssumeRole passes both on
      ⇒ an ask of ahbode/infrastructure: the trust statement on '<role>'
        for this box's principal must allow all three at once:
        "sts:AssumeRole", "sts:SetSourceIdentity", "sts:TagSession"
      ⇒ read the refusal in full, on the box (it names the ids):
        aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>

## a source-identity refusal
   ✋ ahbode.prep — the role TRUSTS this box, and refuses what its session carries (sts:SetSourceIdentity)
      ⇒ an IAM Roles Anywhere session carries a source identity and session tags,
        and a chained AssumeRole passes both on
      ⇒ an ask of ahbode/infrastructure: the trust statement on '<role>'
        for this box's principal must allow all three at once:
        "sts:AssumeRole", "sts:SetSourceIdentity", "sts:TagSession"
      ⇒ read the refusal in full, on the box (it names the ids):
        aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>

## a bare AssumeRole refusal
   ✋ ahbode.prep — the hop is declared, and this box is REFUSED it
      ⇒ a re-apply of this bundle refuses identically
      ⇒ TWO causes wear this one message, and they want OPPOSITE repairs:
      1. does a 'ahbode' row belong on a grove of THIS org at all?
         no  ⇒ 🔴 OURS. delete the row; no grant is owed, and none may
               be sought (rule.require.a-grove-reaches-its-own-org-only)
      2. only if yes — the role EXISTS and this box sits outside its
         trust policy ⇒ an ask of ahbode/infrastructure: trust this box's
         principal on '<role>', with all three actions at once:
         "sts:AssumeRole", "sts:SetSourceIdentity", "sts:TagSession"
      ⇒ ask 1 FIRST. its answer is the ORG's, and the refusal says no
        word about it — an ask filed on a no buys a durable hop into
        another org's accounts, to silence a check that was right
      ⇒ read the refusal in full, on the box (it names the ids):
        aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>

## a profile aws cannot find
   ✋ the rack names '<profile>' for ahbode.prep, and it does not answer
      ⇒ a named profile with no live body is a profile aws cannot find
        — the half-applied pair aws.reach.set exists to prevent
      ⇒ read the refusal in full:
        aws sts get-caller-identity --profile <profile>
      fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.13.reach --mode apply


